# Environment schema for the discordkit Gateway Event Inspector.
#
# This file is COMMITTED and must never contain real secret values — it only
# declares the shape and rules. Put real values in a local `.env` (gitignored).
# Varlock validates against this schema and redacts anything marked @sensitive
# from logs.
#
# `varlock-wrangler dev` resolves these and injects them into miniflare as
# ordinary Worker bindings; `varlock-wrangler deploy` attaches non-sensitive
# values as Cloudflare vars and sensitive ones as Cloudflare secrets.
#
# NOTE: this example deliberately does NOT use `@varlock/cloudflare-integration`'s
# in-Worker `ENV` import. That requires the `nodejs_compat` compatibility flag,
# and proving @discordkit/gateway runs on the BARE Workers runtime is the whole
# point here (`vp run check:bundle` fails the build if a Node builtin appears).
# The CLI wrapper runs in Node outside the Worker, so we get schema validation,
# .env watching, and the vars-vs-secrets split without the runtime dependency.
# The Worker just reads the plain binding varlock injects.

# @defaultRequired=false
# @defaultSensitive=true
# ---

# Your Discord bot token (Developer Portal → Bot → Reset Token).
#
# Optional: the inspector's UI takes a token at connect time, so the app runs
# without this. Set it only if you'd rather not paste the token into the form
# each time. It is never sent to the browser — the Durable Object holds it and
# opens the Gateway connection server-side.
#
# @sensitive=true
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Overrides the Gateway URL. Only for pointing the inspector at a mock gateway;
# leave unset to connect to Discord.
# @sensitive=false
GATEWAY_URL=
